.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "BSDSF23M009-OS-A01" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search for a string pattern within a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches );
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function searches each line of the given file stream
.I fp
for occurrences of
.I search_str,
and fills the
.I matches
array with the matching lines.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matches found, or -1 on failure.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Alisha (BSDSF23M009).
